Security: A custom instance name is escaped in the page body and in HTML mails

The name of the instance can be set freely (theme app, occ, or imported
from the previous generation during a migration). The page layouts printed it
unescaped into the class attribute of the body element on every page,
including the public login page, and the HTML mail footer as well as the new
user mail inserted it unescaped into the text. A name with quotes broke the
markup, a name with markup ended up as HTML. All these places escape the name
now.

If an instance carries its own name, the trademark sentence of the mail
footer names owncloud.online explicitly instead of the customer's name.
